# Test: the support archive carries the kernel artifact and the readiness block.
# VALIDATES: AC-8 of spec-crash-capture -- `ze support --module crashes` emits
#            each report with its kind and full content, plus the readiness
#            block, through the existing `crashes` module. No new module name.
# PREVENTS: a bundle that is ambiguous about a box with no kernel report. An
#           engineer reading the archive cannot tell "never faulted" from "was
#           never armed" out of a file list, and readiness is the field that
#           answers it.
option=env:var=ze.crash.dir:value=crashdir

tmpfs=crashdir/crash-20260905-110000-dmesg-ramoops-0-kernel.log:terminator=EOF_KERNEL
=== Ze Crash Report ===
Time: 2026-09-05T11:00:00Z

=== Kernel Crash ===
Kind: kernel
Record: dmesg-ramoops-0

Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt
EOF_KERNEL

# The archive is written into the per-test working dir (--output .), which the
# runner allocates fresh and cleans up.
tmpfs=.support-out-keep:terminator=EOF_KEEP
placeholder so the runner allocates an isolated working dir
EOF_KEEP

# `--json` prints the manifest and only the manifest: one {collected,
# duration-ms} row per module (SupportManifest, internal/component/support/
# support.go). The reports and the readiness block are in the ARCHIVE, so the
# second command reads crashes.json back out of it and the assertions below it
# hold on the bytes ze wrote there.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze support --module crashes --json --output .:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains="crashes"
expect=stdout:contains="collected": true

# `expect=exit:code=` is what makes the runner WAIT for this command: a
# foreground helper that is the last line of a file is otherwise started and
# torn down without a Wait, and its stdout races the assertions below
# (runOrchestrated, internal/test/runner/runner_exec.go).
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture plugin/support-crashes-archive
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="kind": "kernel"
expect=stdout:contains="readiness"
expect=stdout:contains=Kernel panic - not syncing
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
